cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use agentcourier in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "agentcourier: encrypted messages and files between AI agents across machines"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hermann
    given-names: Alexander
version: 2.3.1
date-released: 2026-11-14
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/alhermann/agentcourier"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/agentcourier/"
abstract: >-
  agentcourier is an MCP server that lets AI coding agents such as Claude Code,
  Codex and GitHub Copilot exchange messages and files: between sessions on one
  computer, across a user's machines (including HPC clusters), and with
  colleagues' machines. It needs no account or cloud service; machines are paired
  once, and every connection between machines is end-to-end encrypted with a
  post-quantum hybrid key exchange.
keywords:
  - model context protocol
  - AI agents
  - agent-to-agent communication
  - HPC
  - end-to-end encryption
